# Scale Standards

## Capacity language
- Translate goals into measurable units: peak **RPS**, concurrent connections, data growth/month, queue depth.
- Plan headroom **2–3×** expected peak. Load-test before campaigns/launches.

## Scale-out defaults
- Stateless app tier behind a load balancer; session state in Redis/DB if needed.
- Autoscale on CPU/RPS/queue lag — with cool-down to avoid flapping.
- DB scale: vertical + read replicas first; partition/shard only with evidence and re-shard plan.

## Absorbing spikes
- Queue writes that can wait; shed non-critical load; serve stale/cached reads when degraded.
- Rate-limit at edge and app. Backpressure > blind retry storms.
- Idempotent consumers so scaled workers can retry safely.

## Growth checklist
- Before 10× traffic: indexes reviewed, pool sizes tuned, caches warm strategy, multi-AZ, backup restore tested.
- Track unit cost per request/user; reject linearly expensive designs without need.
